{"id": "whmanu", "name": "Manú National Park", "short": "Manú", "place": "Peru", "lat": -11.86, "lon": -71.72, "side": "l", "cont": "South America", "country": "Peru", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Cloud forest to Amazon lowland: jaguars, giant otters and macaws.", "tip": {"id": "lick", "title": "Close the clay licks", "text": "Macaws gather at riverbank clay licks to eat soil. Set Clay licks to -100% and watch the scarlet macaw, then the fruit trees it feeds on."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Manú National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manú_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Brown woolly monkey", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_woolly_monkey"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Giant otter", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_otter"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Jaguar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Spectacled bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spectacled_bear"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Andean cock-of-the-rock", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andean_cock-of-the-rock"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Manú National Park", "icon": "lion", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "fig", "sp": "ficus", "xh": 0.1, "name": "Figs", "desc": "Strangler and tree figs bear fruit that many forest animals eat; GloBI records link fig fruit to woolly monkeys, pacas and brockets near Manú.", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "brosimum", "sp": "brosimum lactescens", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "bromeliad", "sp": "bromeliaceae", "xh": 0.55}, {"id": "laurel", "sp": "ocotea", "xh": 0.8}, {"id": "woolly", "sp": "lagothrix lagothricha", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "tapir", "sp": "tapirus terrestris", "xh": 0.2, "name": "South American tapir", "wiki": "South American tapir", "desc": "A big lowland forest browser and fruit-eater. It is a large prey animal for jaguars in GloBI records."}, {"id": "paca", "sp": "cuniculus paca", "xh": 0.33, "desc": "A forest rodent that eats fallen fruit such as figs, and is itself prey for jaguars.", "ic": "vole"}, {"id": "peccary", "sp": "tayassu pecari", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "Roams the forest in herds, rooting for fruit and seeds. Jaguars are recorded preying on it."}, {"id": "macaw", "sp": "ara macao", "xh": 0.59, "desc": "A fruit and seed-eating parrot. Macaws gather at riverbank clay licks in the western Amazon, which is a big draw for visitors to Manú.", "ic": "hawk"}, {"id": "cock", "sp": "rupicola peruvianus", "xh": 0.72}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "tremarctos ornatus", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "fish", "sp": "characiformes", "xh": 0.95}, {"id": "otter", "sp": "pteronura brasiliensis", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "Family groups hunt fish, mainly characins, in shallow water. Black caimans have been reported preying on them."}, {"id": "caiman", "sp": "melanosuchus niger", "xh": 0.45, "tl": 3, "desc": "A large lowland river and oxbow-lake predator that eats fish and has been reported taking giant otters in Peru."}, {"id": "condor", "sp": "vultur gryphus", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "A scavenging bird of the high Andes that glides over the park's highland zone and feeds on carrion."}, {"id": "jaguar", "sp": "panthera onca", "xh": 0.25, "desc": "The top predator of the lowland forest, eating prey from fish and caiman to peccary and tapir."}, {"id": "puma", "sp": "puma concolor", "xh": 0.55, "desc": "A big cat found from lowland to montane forest. It can prey on spectacled bear cubs."}, {"id": "harpy", "sp": "harpia harpyja", "xh": 0.85, "desc": "A huge forest-canopy eagle that hunts monkeys and sloths. It is listed among the lowland birds of Manú."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Drives growth from the warm lowlands to the cloud-forest slopes."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rain and cloud mist", "xh": 0.32}, {"